<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sonsonate</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sonsonate is a city in western El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> and capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of the same name. In the colonial period it was the seat of a separate alcaldía mayor and a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a> trade. In 1834 it briefly served as the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a> before the federal government moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-salvador">San Salvador</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sonsonate.jpg" alt="Sonsonate" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ronan84 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sonso.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
